  "schema_version": "energy-parametric-known-answers-v0.1",
  "scope": "Frozen two-interval integer-quantized synthetic electrical model only. The first interval has zero load and PV availability equal to the declared PV kW for one hour; the grid is available with declared grid kW. The second interval has a two-kWh essential load, zero PV, and a grid outage. Battery efficiency is idealized at 1.0, initial SOC and terminal reserve are zero, and synthetic grid cost/carbon factors are explicitly zero.",
  "derivation": "For each charge c in 0..=min(battery_capacity_kWh,battery_charge_discharge_power_kW), feasible first-interval grid import g is max(0,c-PV)..=min(grid_power,c). For each (c,g), the second interval has min(c,battery_discharge_power,2)+1 withdrawal/service choices. The non-dominated frontier uses maximum feasible charge C=min(capacity,power), with essential unserved 2-w, curtailment max(PV-C,0), and terminal SOC C-w for w=C..0. These are analytical known answers for this declared discrete model, not real-site estimates.",
